			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@stuffbreaker\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>stuffbreaker</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> “Breaks”? The tag either upgrades or it doesn’t. Breaks is for weaker, less capable client side APIs the need far less frequent version management work. </p><p>But, with different names you could put different ones in different places and get seasonally different experiences. Maybe the confusion season includes A LOT more. Maybe fall and spring deserve different icons. Maybe I’m not pushing hard enough?</p><p>The power is yours!</p>",
